@model bool
@*
    THE race page's main chart: per-rider speed against completion of the course, over the course itself —
    the terrain tinted per section, a rule at every section boundary, the field's own p10–p90 spread, and
    the replay playhead. Rendered by BOTH the owner page and the /s/{token} fork: it is a view, not a
    control, so the two must not drift (see the header of _ShareRaceBody.cshtml).

    It sits directly under the map now, where the dock's elevation strip used to be read. That strip is
    still there and still the live 30 Hz surface for 508 rider dots — but only in FULLSCREEN replay
    (race-replay.css); inline, this is the one picture, because "where the course climbs, the field slows,
    and here is what THESE two riders did about it" was being read across two charts lined up by eye.

    Why it is a panel and not a strip in the dock: it ZOOMS, and the dock is a fixed-height overlay on the
    map's bottom edge — the wrong place to pinch, drag, and click a section boundary into place.

    The model is one bool: whether the viewer may edit. It reaches the canvas's aria-label only — the
    click-to-place behaviour itself is gated in race-replay-view (editable:false on the fork).

    #raceSpeedPanel is the empty-state host and must WRAP the canvas directly — core/chart-empty-state
    finds the canvas by querySelector. Note the panel prefers #raceSpeedNote for "no riders drawn yet",
    precisely so the canvas is NOT hidden: the course, and the boundaries you place on it, must stay.
*@
@* race-panel-speed lifts the panel's overflow clip — the readout box floats above the plot. *@
<section class="race-panel race-panel-speed">
    <div class="race-panel-head">
        <span>Speed</span>
        @* Not an overlay: a race whose sections are still being laid out has no highlighted riders, and
           the canvas has to keep showing the course underneath. *@
        <small class="race-speed-note" id="raceSpeedNote" hidden></small>
        @* Recorded vs smoothed, same control as the activity and segment speed charts. Its own
           preference key, so switching here does not move those. *@
        <button class="chart-mode-toggle" id="raceSpeedModeToggle" type="button" aria-pressed="false"></button>
    </div>
    <div class="race-speed-wrap" id="raceSpeedPanel">
        <canvas id="raceSpeedChart" class="race-speed-chart"
                aria-label="@(Model
                    ? "Speed against completion of the course, over the course profile — click to split a section, drag a boundary to move it"
                    : "Speed against completion of the course, over the course profile, one line per drawn rider")"></canvas>
    </div>
</section>
